What:		/sys/kernel/ki_profile/memory_tuning
Date:		November 2026
Contact:	Ki-kernel maintainers
Description:
		Read/write boolean, default 0. Access permissions are 0644.

		0 leaves VM settings under ROM/userspace control. Boot profile
		application, profile changes and explicit reapply do not write
		watermark_scale_factor, watermark_boost_factor,
		compact_unevictable_allowed or vfs_cache_pressure.

		Writing 1 applies the selected user profile's VM settings
		immediately and enables their application on subsequent forced
		profile updates. Transient screen-off Battery mode does not
		select a different memory policy. Swappiness is never changed.

		Writing 0 stops further profile VM writes; it does not restore
		previous values. Userspace may apply its own values afterwards.
		The setting is not persisted across reboot. CPU, GPU, thermal
		and idle-floor profile controls operate independently.
